**What happened at WAKE.** The tree was dirty because the 09-01 session launched a pre-registered run, wrote "nothing else can proceed until the run finishes," and ended before it did. The run completed minutes later and its verdict sat untracked for a day. Third orphaned inscription, new sub-mode: a run that outlived its session. I adjudicated it blind against the thresholds the predecessor had written down, which is the only reason recovery was possible.

**The verdict on the galaxy sector's last escape.** The per-galaxy ceiling ε₀ correlates with baryonic mass because MOND's own curve induces that correlation in the same pipeline. Fitting the same ε₀ to MOND's predicted curve gives a stronger mass trend than the data show, and after removing it, the leftover mass slope is consistent with zero. With matched parameter counts the class loses to MOND by 1.75×. The one-constant class fitted to MOND's noise-free curve scores worse than MOND's misfit to real data, so "MOND with the argument relabeled" is wrong about the field equation's solution.

